 {"title":"Discuss / Argue — condicional perfeito no seu trabalho","note":"Respostas-modelo C1–C2 que o aluno adapta.","items":[
   {"q":"What past operational decision would you reverse with hindsight?","a":"Had we reviewed the flow mix three years earlier, we would have adopted cross-docking on the fast-moving lines and released a material amount of working capital we instead left tied up in stock."},
   {"q":"How do you quantify a missed opportunity to senior management?","a":"If cross-docking had been implemented when it was first proposed, working capital would have improved by roughly twenty percent, which is the precise figure I use to justify the investment now."},
   {"q":"Why is cross-docking often overlooked despite its impact?","a":"Cross-docking is unglamorous, so it is repeatedly deprioritised, yet had it been in place the accumulation of stock that now constrains us would largely have been avoided."},
   {"q":"Describe how earlier flow segmentation would have helped.","a":"Had we segmented the flow by velocity earlier, the demand variability that periodically overwhelms the warehouse would have been absorbed far more smoothly across the network."},
   {"q":"What does post-mortem reasoning add to your decision-making?","a":"Reasoning in the conditional perfect is not regret but discipline: by showing what the past could have yielded, it converts a missed opportunity into a quantified case for acting now."},
   {"q":"How would tempo as a priority have changed your cash position?","a":"Had tempo been treated as a first-order objective rather than an afterthought, working capital would have been released far earlier and the firm's risk profile would have been correspondingly lighter."}]}
